# Updater environment template
#
# Google sign-in is REQUIRED (D-031): set the three AUTH_* variables below in
# `.env.local` before `npm run dev`. Until they are all set, every page
# redirects to /sign-in, which says sign-in isn't available. Tests, lint,
# type check, and build need no variables. The current code reads the Google
# sign-in block and the optional GITHUB_TOKEN; the other entries are reserved
# for planned integrations (see tracker.md, Phase 10) so names stay consistent.
#
# Rules (see rules.md §7.3):
# - Copy to `.env.local` for local values. `.env.local` is git-ignored.
# - Never commit real secrets.
# - Only variables prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_ are exposed to the browser.
#   Never put a credential behind a NEXT_PUBLIC_ name.

# --- GitHub public repository import (T10.1) — server-only, optional ---
# Without it, GitHub allows 60 API requests per hour for this server's IP
# address, shared by everyone using it (one import uses 1–3). A token raises
# that to 5,000. Use a fine-grained token with no repository access and no
# permissions: only public data is read. It is never sent to the browser.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
# --- Planned: GitHub OAuth (T10.2) — server-only ---
# OAuth app credentials for the future "Connect GitHub" flow.
# GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
# GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Google sign-in (T10.5) — server-only, required ---
# All three are needed. Each Google account gets its own workspace.
# Restart the server after changing them.
#
# Random secret that encrypts the session cookie. Generate one with:
#   openssl rand -base64 33
# AUTH_SECRET=
# OAuth client from Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → Credentials →
# "OAuth client ID" (type: Web application). Authorized redirect URI:
#   http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/google   (development)
#   https://<your-domain>/api/auth/callback/google   (production)
# AUTH_GOOGLE_ID=
# AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET=
# Self-hosting behind `npm run start` (not Vercel): trust the Host header,
# or set AUTH_URL to the public origin instead.
# AUTH_TRUST_HOST=true
# AUTH_URL=https://<your-domain>

# --- Planned: AI-assisted drafting (T10.7) — server-only, always optional ---
# AI_PROVIDER_API_KEY=
